repository-code: "https://github.com/stegani/tessera"
abstract: >-
  Tessera is a programming language designed to be written mainly by artificial
  intelligence and to resist attackers that are themselves AI: declared effects,
  resources as unique permissions, verified contracts, and untrusted data kept
  distinct in the type system. It is aimed especially at local models, which gain
  the most from a language where the compiler stops mistakes. This prototype
  includes the grammar, an interpreter with static checks, a WebAssembly compiler
  for pure functions, and an experiment comparing Tessera with Python.
keywords:
  - programming language
  - AI safety
  - security by construction
  - formal verification
  - WebAssembly
  - local AI
